2. You may use the upright or the low handles for cet exercice. Place vos mains on the handles with vos bras extended, leaning into the implement.
3. With good posture, drive through the ground with alternating, short steps. Move as fast as you can for a short distance.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Pectoraux, Fessiers, Quadriceps, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Prowler_Sprint/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Pull Through', 'Fessiers', 'Poulie', '1. Begin standing a few feet in front of a low pulley with a rope or handle attached. Face away from the machine, straddling the cable, with vos pieds set wide apart.
2. Begin le mouvement by reaching through vos jambes as far as possible, bending at the hanches. Keep your genous slightly bent. Keeping vos bras straight, extend through the hanche to stand straight up. Avoid pulling upward through the épaules; all of the motion should originate through the hanches.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Pull_Through/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Pullups', 'Dos', 'Poids de corps', '1. Grab the pull-up bar with the paumes vers l''avant using the prescribed grip. Note on grips: For a prise large, vos mains need to be spaced out at a distance wider than your épaule width. For a prise moyenne, vos mains need to be spaced out at a distance equal to your épaule width and for a close grip at a distance smaller than your épaule width.
2. As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar at the chosen grip width, bring your torse back around 30 degrees or so while creating a curvature on your lower back and sticking your poitrine out. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Pull your torse up until the bar touches your upper poitrine by drawing the épaules and the upper arms down and back. Expirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torse should remain stationary as it moves through space and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar.
4. After a second on the contracted position, start to inspirez and Lentement, lower your torse back to the position de départ when vos bras are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched.
5. Répétez this motion for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Pullups/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Push-Up Wide', 'Pectoraux', 'Poids de corps', '1. With vos mains wide apart, support votre corps on your toes and hands in a plank position. Your coudes should be extended and votre corps straight. Do not allow your hanches to sag. C''est votre position de départ.
2. To begin, allow the coudes to flex, lowering your poitrine to le sol as you inspirez.
3. Using your pectoral muscles, press your upper body back up to the position de départ by extending the coudes. Expirez as you perform this step.
4. After pausing at the contracted position, Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Push-Up_Wide/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Push-Ups - Close Triceps Position', 'Triceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol face down and place vos mains closer than épaule width for a close hand position. Make sure that you are holding your torse up at arms'' length.
2. Lower yourself until your poitrine almost touches le sol as you inspirez.
3. Using your triceps and some of your pectoral muscles, press your upper body back up to the position de départ and squeeze your poitrine. Expirez as you perform this step.
4. Après une pause, at the contracted position, Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Push-Ups_-_Close_Triceps_Position/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Push-Ups With Feet Elevated', 'Pectoraux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol face down and place vos mains about 36 inches apart from each other holding your torse up bras tendus.
2. Place your toes on top of a flat banc. This will allow votre corps to be elevated. Note: The higher the elevation of the flat banc, the higher the resistance of the exercise is.
3. Lower yourself until your poitrine almost touches le sol as you inspirez.
4. Using your pectoral muscles, press your upper body back up to the position de départ and squeeze your poitrine. Expirez as you perform this step.
5. Après une pause, at the contracted position, Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Push-Ups_With_Feet_Elevated/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Push-Ups With Feet On An Exercise Ball', 'Pectoraux', 'Swiss ball', '1. Allongez-vous au sol face down and place vos mains about 36 inches apart from each other holding your torse up bras tendus.
2. Place your toes on top of an exercise ball. This will allow votre corps to be elevated.
3. Lower yourself until your poitrine almost touches le sol as you inspirez.
4. Using your pectoral muscles, press your upper body back up to the position de départ and squeeze your poitrine. Expirez as you perform this step.
5. Après une pause, at the contracted position, Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Push-Ups_With_Feet_On_An_Exercise_Ball/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Push Press', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '', 'Muscles secondaires : Quadriceps, Triceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Push_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Push Press - Behind the Neck', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Standing with the poids racked on the back of the épaules, begin with the dip. With vos pieds directly under your hanches, flex the genous without moving the hanches backward. Go down only slightly, and reverse direction as powerfully as possible. Drive through the heels create as much speed and force as possible, moving the bar in a vertical path.
2. Using the momentum generated, finish pressing the poids overhead be extending through the arms.
3. Revenez en position de départ, using vos jambes to absorb the impact.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Quadriceps, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Push_Press_-_Behind_the_Neck/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Push Up to Side Plank', 'Pectoraux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Get into pushup position on the toes with vos mains just outside of épaule width.
2. Perform a pushup by allowing the coudes to flex. As you descend, keep votre corps straight.
3. Do one pushup and as you come up, shift your poids on the left side of the body, twist to the side while bringing the right arm up towards the ceiling in a side plank.
4. Lower the arm back to le sol for another pushup and then twist to the other side.
5. Répétez the series, alternating each side, for 10 or more reps.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Push_Up_to_Side_Plank/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Pushups', 'Pectoraux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol face down and place vos mains about 36 inches apart while holding your torse up bras tendus.
2. Next, lower yourself downward until your poitrine almost touches le sol as you inspirez.
3. Now Expirez and press your upper body back up to the position de départ while squeezing your poitrine.
4. Après une pause, at the top contracted position, you can begin to lower yourself downward again for as many repetitions as needed.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Pushups/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Pushups (Close and Wide Hand Positions)', 'Pectoraux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol face down and body straight with your toes on le sol and the hands wider than épaule width for a wide hand position and closer than épaule width for a close hand position. Make sure you are holding your torse up bras tendus.
2. Lower yourself until your poitrine almost touches le sol as you inspirez.
3. Using your pectoral muscles, press your upper body back up to the position de départ and squeeze your poitrine. Expirez as you perform this step.
4. Après une pause, at the contracted position, Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Pushups_Close_and_Wide_Hand_Positions/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Pyramid', 'Bas du dos', 'Swiss ball', '1. Start off by rolling your torse forward onto the ball so your hanches rest on top of the ball and become the highest point of votre corps.
2. Rest vos mains and feet on le sol. vos bras and legs can be slightly bent or straight, depending on the size of the ball, your flexibility, and the length of your limbs. This also helps develop stabilizing strength in your torse and épaules.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Pyramid/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Quad Stretch', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Lay on your side. Loop a belt, rope, or band around your top foot. Flex the genou and extend your hanche, attempting to touch your fessiers with your foot, and holding the belt with vos mains. C''est votre position de départ.
2. With the belt being held over the épaule or overhead, gently pull to increase the stretch in the quadriceps. Maintenez 10-20 secondes, and then switch sides.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Quad_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Quadriceps-SMR', 'Quadriceps', 'Foam roller', '1. Lay facedown on le sol with your poids supported by vos mains or forearms. Place a foam roll underneath one leg on the quadriceps, and keep the foot off of the ground. Make sure to relax the leg as much as possible. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Shifting as much poids onto the leg to be stretched as is tolerable, roll over the foam from above the genou to below the hanche, holding points of tension for 10-30 seconds. Switch sides.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Quadriceps-SMR/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Quick Leap', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. You will need a box for this exerise.
2. Begin facing the box standing 1-2 feet from its edge.
3. By utilizing your hanches, hop onto the box, landing on both legs. Ensure that you land with vos jambes bent and vos pieds flat.
4. Immediately upon landing, fully extend through the entire body and swing vos bras overhead to explode off of the box. Use vos jambes to absorb the impact of landing.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Quick_Leap/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rack Delivery', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. This drill teaches the delivery of the barre to the rack position on the épaules. Begin holding a bar in the scarecrow position, with the upper arms parallèle au sol, and the forearms hanging down. Use a hook grip, with your fingers wrapped over your thumbs.
2. Begin by rotating the coudes around the bar, delivering the bar to the épaules. As your coudes come forward, relax your grip. The épaules should be protracted, providing a shelf for the bar, which should lightly contact the throat.
3. It is important that the bar stay close to the body en permanence, as with a heavier load any distance will result in an unwanted collision. As le mouvement becomes smoother, speed and load can be increased before progressing further.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rack_Delivery/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rack Pull with Bands', 'Bas du dos', 'Barre', '1. Set up in a power rack with the bar on the pins. The pins should be set to the desired point; just below the genous, just above, or in the mid cuisse position. Attach bands to the base of the rack, or secure them with haltères. Attach the other end to the bar. You may need to choke the bands to provide tension.
2. Position yourself against the bar in proper deadlifting position. vos pieds should be under your hanches, your grip épaule width, back arched, and hanches back to engage the ischio-jambiers. Since the poids is typically heavy, you may use a mixed grip, a hook grip, or use straps to aid in holding the poids.
3. With votre tête looking forward, extend through the hanches and genous, pulling the poids up and back until lockout. Be sure to pull your épaules back as you complete le mouvement. Return the poids to the pins and Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rack_Pull_with_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rack Pulls', 'Bas du dos', 'Barre', '1. Set up in a power rack with the bar on the pins. The pins should be set to the desired point; just below the genous, just above, or in the mid cuisse position. Position yourself against the bar in proper deadlifting position. vos pieds should be under your hanches, your grip épaule width, back arched, and hanches back to engage the ischio-jambiers. Since the poids is typically heavy, you may use a mixed grip, a hook grip, or use straps to aid in holding the poids.
2. With votre tête looking forward, extend through the hanches and genous, pulling the poids up and back until lockout. Be sure to pull your épaules back as you complete le mouvement.
3. Return the poids to the pins and Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rack_Pulls/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rear Leg Raises', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Place yourself on vos mains genous on an exercise mat. votre tête should be looking forward and the bend of the genous should create a angle de 90 degrés between the ischio-jambiers and the mollets. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Extend one leg up and behind you. The genou and hanche should both extend. Répétez for 5-10 repetitions, and then switch sides.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rear_Leg_Raises/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Recumbent Bike', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, seat yourself on the bike and adjust the seat to your height.
2. Select the desired option from the menu. You may have to start pedaling to turn it on. You can use the manual setting, or you can select a program to use. Typically, you can enter your age and poids to estimate the amount of calories burned during exercise. The level of resistance can be changed throughout the workout. The handles can be used to monitor your heart rate to help you stay at an appropriate intensity.
3. Recumbent bikes offer convenience, cardiovascular benefits, and have less impact than other activities. A 150 lb person will burn about 230 calories cycling at a moderate rate for 30 minutes, compared to 450 calories or more running.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Recumbent_Bike/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Return Push from Stance', 'Épaules', 'Medecine ball', '1. You will need a partner for this drill.
2. Begin in an athletic 2 or 3 point stance.
3. At the signal, move into a position to receive the pass from your partner.
4. Catch the medicine ball with both hands and immediately throw it back to your partner.
5. You can modify this drill by running different routes.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Return_Push_from_Stance/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Band Bench Press', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. Position a banc inside a power rack, with the bar set to the correct height. Begin by anchoring bands either to band pegs or to the top of the rack. Ensure that you will be position properly under the bands. Attach the other end to the barre.
2. Lie on the banc, tuck vos pieds underneath you and arch votre dos. Using the bar to help support your poids, lift your épaule off the banc and retract them, squeezing the omoplates together. Use vos pieds to drive your traps into the banc. Maintain this tight body position throughout le mouvement. However wide your grip, it should cover the ring on the bar.
3. Pull the bar out of the rack without protracting your épaules. Focus on squeezing the bar and trying to pull it apart. Lower the bar to your lower poitrine or upper stomach. The bar, poignet, and coude should stay in line en permanence.
4. Pause when the barre touches your torse, and then drive the bar up with as much force as possible. The coudes should be tucked in until lockout.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Avant-bras, Dos, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Band_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Band Box Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Begin in a power rack with a box at the appropriate height behind you. Set up the bands either on band pegs or attached to the top of the rack, ensuring they will be directly above the bar during the squat. Attach the other end to the bar.
2. Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the épaules. Squeeze your omoplates together and rotate your coudes forward, attempting to bend the bar across your épaules. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back, and step back into position. Place vos pieds wider for more emphasis on the back, fessiers, adductors, and ischio-jambiers, or closer together for more quad development. Keep votre tête facing forward.
3. With votre dos, épaules, and sangle abdominale tight, push your genous and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hanches until you are seated on the box. Ideally, your shins should be perpendiculaire à the ground. Pause when you reach the box, and relax the hanche flexors. Never bounce off of a box.
4. Keeping the poids on your heels and pushing vos pieds and genous out, drive upward off of the box as you lead le mouvement with votre tête. Continue upward, maintaining tightness head to toe. Use care to return the barre to the rack.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Band_Box_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Band Deadlift', 'Bas du dos', 'Barre', '1. Set the bar up in a power rack. Attach bands to the top of the rack, using either bands pegs or the frame itself. Attach the other end of the bands to the bar.
2. Approach the bar so that it is centered over vos pieds. You feet should be about hanche width apart. Bend at the hanche to grip the bar at épaule width, allowing your omoplates to protract. Typically, you would use an prise en pronation or an over/under grip on heavier sets.
3. With vos pieds, and your grip set, take a big breath and then lower your hanches and bend the genous until your shins contact the bar. Look forward with votre tête, keep your poitrine up and votre dos arched, and begin driving through the heels to move the poids upward.
4. After the bar passes the genous, aggressively pull the bar back, pulling your omoplates together as you drive your hanches forward into the bar.
5. Lower the bar by bending at the hanches and guiding it to le sol.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Quadriceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Band_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Band Power Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Begin in a power rack with the pins and bar set at the appropriate height. After loading the bar, attach bands to the top of the rack, using either pegs or the frame itself. Attach the other end of the bands to the bar.
2. Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the épaules. Squeeze your omoplates together and rotate your coudes forward, attempting to bend the bar across your épaules. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back, and step back into position. Place vos pieds wide for more emphasis on the back, fessiers, adductors, and ischio-jambiers.
3. Keep votre tête facing forward. With votre dos, épaules, and sangle abdominale tight, push your genous and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hanches as much as possible. Ideally, your shins should be perpendiculaire à the ground. Lower bar position necessitates a greater torse lean to keep the bar over the heels. Continue until you break parallel, which is defined as the crease of the hanche being in line with the top of the genou.
4. Keeping the poids on your heels and pushing vos pieds and genous out, drive upward as you lead le mouvement with votre tête. Continue upward, maintaining tightness head to toe, until you have returned to the position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Band_Power_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Band Sumo Deadlift', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a bar loaded on le sol inside of a power rack. Attach bands to the top of the rack, using either pegs or the frame itself. Attach the other end to the barre.
2. Approach the bar so that the bar intersects the middle of the feet. The feet should be set very wide, near the collars. Bend at the hanches to grip the bar. The arms should be directly below the épaules, inside the legs, and you can use a pronated grip, a mixed grip, or hook grip. Relax the épaules, which in effect lengthens vos bras.
3. Take a breath, and then lower your hanches, looking forward with votre tête with your poitrine up. Drive through le sol, spreading vos pieds apart, with your poids on the back half of vos pieds. Extend through the hanches and genous.
4. As the bar passes through the genous, lean back and drive the hanches into the bar, pulling your omoplates together.
5. Return the poids to the ground by bending at the hanches and controlling the poids on the way down.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Band_Sumo_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Barbell Curl', 'Biceps', 'Barre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse upright while holding a barre at épaule width with the coudes close to the torse. The palm of vos mains should be facing down (pronated grip). C''est votre position de départ.
2. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the poids while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the bar is at épaule level. Maintenez la position 1 seconde as you squeeze the muscle.
3. Lentement, begin to bring the bar back to position de départ as your Inspirez.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Barbell_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Barbell Preacher Curls', 'Biceps', 'Barre EZ', '1. Grab an EZ-bar using a épaule width and palms down (pronated) grip.
2. Now place the upper part of both arms on top of the preacher banc and have vos bras extended. C''est votre position de départ.
3. As you expirez, use the biceps to curl the poids up until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the barre is at épaule height. Squeeze the biceps hard for a second at the contracted position.
4. As you Inspirez, Lentement, lower the barre until your upper arms are extended and the biceps is fully stretched.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Barbell_Preacher_Curls/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Cable Curl', 'Biceps', 'Poulie', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse upright while holding a bar attachment that is attached to a low pulley using a pronated (palms down) and épaule width grip. Make sure also that you keep the coudes close to the torse. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the poids while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the bar is at épaule level. Maintenez la position 1 seconde as you squeeze the muscle.
3. Lentement, begin to bring the bar back to position de départ as your Inspirez.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Cable_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol with vos jambes fully extended and arms to the side of your torse with the palms on le sol. vos bras should be stationary for the entire exercise.
2. Move vos jambes up so that your cuisses are perpendiculaire à le sol and feet are together and parallèle au sol. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While inhaling, move vos jambes towards the torse as you roll your pelvis backwards and you raise your hanches off le sol. At the end of this movement your genous will be touching your poitrine.
4. Hold the contraction for a second and move vos jambes back to the position de départ while exhaling.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Flyes', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. To begin, lie down on an incline banc with the poitrine and stomach pressing against the incline. Have the haltères in each hand with the paumes vers each other (neutral grip).
2. Extend the arms in front of you so that they are perpendiculaire à the angle of the banc. The legs should be stationary while applying pressure with the ball of your toes. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Maintaining the slight bend of the coudes, move the poids out and away from each other (to the side) in an arc motion while exhaling. Conseil : Try to squeeze your omoplates together to get the best results from cet exercice.
4. The arms should be elevated until they are parallèle au sol.
5. Feel the contraction and Lentement, lower the poids back down to the position de départ while inhaling.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Flyes/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Flyes With External Rotation', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. To begin, lie down on an incline banc set at a angle de 30 degrés with the poitrine and stomach pressing against the incline.
2. Have the haltères in each hand with the paumes vers down to le sol. vos bras should be in front of you so that they are perpendiculaire à the angle of the banc. Conseil : Your coudes should have a slight bend. The legs should be stationary while applying pressure with the ball of your toes (your heels should not be touching le sol). C''est votre position de départ.
3. Maintaining the slight bend of the coudes, move the poids out and away from each other in an arc motion while exhaling.
4. As you lift the poids, your poignet should externally rotate by 90-degrees so that you go from a palms down (pronated) grip to a paumes vers each other (neutral) grip. Conseil : Try to squeeze your omoplates together to get the best results from cet exercice.
5. The arms should be elevated until they are level with the head.
6. Feel the contraction and Lentement, lower the poids back down to the position de départ while inhaling.
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Flyes_With_External_Rotation/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Grip Bent-Over Rows', 'Milieu du dos', 'Barre', '1. Stand erect while holding a barre with a supinated grip (paumes vers up).
2. Bend your genous slightly and bring your torse forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallèle au sol. Conseil : Make sure that you keep the head up. The barre should hang directly in front of you as vos bras hang perpendiculaire à le sol and your torse. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While keeping the torse stationary, lift the barre as you Expirez, keeping the coudes close to the body and not doing any force with the forearm other than holding the poids. On the top contracted position, squeeze the back muscles and Maintenez la position 1 seconde.
4. Lentement, lower the poids again to the position de départ as you inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Grip_Bent-Over_Rows/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Grip Triceps Pushdown', 'Triceps', 'Poulie', '1. Start by setting a bar attachment (straight or e-z) on a high pulley machine.
2. Facing the bar attachment, grab it with the paumes vers up (supinated grip) at épaule width. Lower the bar by using your lats until vos bras are fully extended by your sides. Conseil : coudes should be in by your sides and vos pieds should be épaule width apart from each other. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lentement, elevate the bar attachment up as you inspirez so it is aligned with your poitrine. Only the forearms should move and the coudes/upper arms should be stationary by your side en permanence.
4. Then begin to lower the cable bar back down to the original staring position while exhaling and contracting the triceps hard.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Grip_Triceps_Pushdown/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Hyperextension', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Machine', '1. Place vos pieds between the pads after loading an appropriate poids. Lay on the top pad, allowing your hanches to hang off the back, while grasping the handles to hold your position.
2. To begin le mouvement, flex the hanches, pulling the legs forward.
3. Reverse the motion by extending the hanches, kicking the leg back. It is very important not to over-extend the hanche on this movement, stopping short of your full range of motion.
4. Return by again flexing the hanche, pulling the carriage forward as far as you can.
5. Répétez for the desired number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Hyperextension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Machine Flyes', 'Épaules', 'Machine', '1. Adjust the handles so that they are fully to the rear. Make an appropriate poids selection and adjust the seat height so the handles are at épaule level. Grasp the handles with vos mains facing inwards. C''est votre position de départ.
2. In a semicircular motion, pull vos mains out to your side and back, contracting your rear delts.
3. Keep vos bras slightly bent throughout le mouvement, with all of the motion occurring at the épaule joint.
4. Pause at the rear of le mouvement, and Lentement, return the poids to the position de départ.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Machine_Flyes/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Plate Curls', 'Biceps', 'Autre', '1. Start by standing straight with a weighted plate held by both hands and arms fully extended. Use a pronated grip (paumes vers down) and make sure your fingers grab the rough side of the plate while your thumb grabs the smooth side. Note: For the best results, grab the weighted plate at an 11:00 and 1:00 o''clock position.
2. vos pieds should be épaule width apart from each other and the weighted plate should be near the groin area. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lentement, lift the plate up while keeping the coudes in and the upper arms stationary until your biceps and forearms touch while exhaling. The plate should be evenly aligned with your torse at this point.
4. Feel the contraction for a second and begin to lower the poids back down to the position de départ while inhaling
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Plate_Curls/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Reverse Triceps Bench Press', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol on a flat banc. Using a close, supinated grip (around épaule width), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras locked extended in front of you and perpendiculaire à le sol. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you Inspirez, come down Lentement, until you feel the bar on your middle poitrine. Conseil : Make sure that as opposed to a regular banc press, you keep the coudes close to the torse en permanence in order to maximize triceps involvement.
3. Après une pause, bring the bar back to the position de départ as you Expirez and push the bar using your triceps muscles. Lock vos bras in the contracted position, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then start coming down Lentement, again. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.
4. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
5. When you are done, place the bar back in the rack.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Reverse_Triceps_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rhomboids-SMR', 'Milieu du dos', 'Foam roller', '1. Lay down with votre dos on le sol. Place a foam roll underneath your upper back, and cross vos bras in front of you, protracting your épaules. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Raise your hanches off of the ground, placing your poids onto the foam roll. Shift your poids to one side at a time, rolling over your middle and upper back. Pause at points of tension for 10-30 seconds.', 'Muscles secondaires : Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rhomboids-SMR/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rickshaw Carry', 'Avant-bras', 'Autre', '1. Position the frame at the starting point, and load with the appropriate poids. Standing in the center of the frame, begin by gripping the handles and driving through your heels to lift the frame. Ensure your poitrine and head are up and votre dos is straight.
2. Immediately begin walking briskly with quick, controlled steps. Keep your poitrine up and head forward, and make sure you continue breathing. Bring the frame to the ground after you have reached the end point.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rickshaw_Carry/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rickshaw Deadlift', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Load the frame with the desired poids. Center yourself between the handles. You feet should be about hanche width apart. Bend at the hanches to grip the handles, allowing your omoplates to protract.
2. With vos pieds and your grip set, take a big breath and then lower your hanches and flex the genous. Look forward with votre tête, keep your poitrine up and votre dos arched, and begin driving through the heels to move the poids upward. As the poids comes up, pull your omoplates together as you drive your hanches forward.
3. Lower the poids by bending at the hanches and guiding it to the ground.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rickshaw_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Ring Dips', 'Triceps', 'Autre', '1. Grip a ring in each hand, and then take a small jump to help you get into the position de départ with vos bras locked out.
2. Begin by flexing the coude, lowering votre corps until vos bras break 90 degrees. Avoid swinging, and maintain good posture throughout the descent.
3. Reverse the motion by extending the coude, pushing yourself back up into the position de départ.
4. Répétez for the desired number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Ring_Dips/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rocket Jump', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin in a relaxed stance with vos pieds épaule width apart and hold vos bras close to the body.
2. To initiate the move, squat down halfway and explode back up as high as possible.
3. Fully extend your entire body, reaching overhead as far as possible. As you land, absorb your impact through the legs.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rocket_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rocking Standing Calf Raise', 'Mollets', 'Barre', '1. cet exercice is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place it on the back of your épaules (slightly below the neck).
2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse.
3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a épaule width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep votre tête up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance. Also maintain a straight back and keep the genous with a slight bend; never locked. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Raise your heels as you Expirez by extending your chevilles as high as possible and flexing your calf. Ensure that the genou is kept stationary en permanence. There should be no bending (other than the slight initial bend we created during positioning) at any time. Hold the contracted position by a second before you start to go back down.
5. Go back Lentement, to the position de départ as you Inspirez by lowering your heels as you bend the chevilles until mollets are stretched.
6. Now lift your toes by contracting the tibia muscles in the front of the mollets as you Expirez.
7. Maintenez la position 1 seconde and bring them back down as you Inspirez.
8. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rocking_Standing_Calf_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rocky Pull-Ups/Pulldowns', 'Dos', 'Autre', '1. Grab the pull-up bar with the paumes vers l''avant using a prise large.
2. As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar at the chosen grip width, bring your torse back around 30 degrees or so while creating a curvature on your lower back and sticking your poitrine out. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Pull your torse up until the bar touches your upper poitrine by drawing the épaules and the upper arms down and back. Expirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torse should remain stationary as it moves through space and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar.
4. After a second on the contracted position, start to inspirez and Lentement, lower your torse back to the position de départ when vos bras are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched.
5. Now Répétez the same movements as described above except this time your torse will remain straight as you go up and the bar will touch the back of the neck instead of the upper poitrine. Conseil : Use the head to lean forward slightly as it will help you properly execute this portion of the exercise.
6. Once you have lowered yourself back down to the position de départ, Répétez the exercise for the prescribed amount of repetitions in your program.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rocky_Pull-Ups_Pulldowns/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Romanian Deadlift', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Put a barre in front of you on the ground and grab it using a pronated (paumes vers down) grip that a little wider than épaule width. Conseil : Depending on the poids used, you may need poignet wraps to perform the exercise and also a raised platform in order to allow for better range of motion.
2. Bend the genous slightly and keep the shins vertical, hanches back and back straight. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping votre dos and arms completely straight en permanence, use your hanches to lift the bar as you expirez. Conseil : le mouvement should not be fast but steady and under control.
4. Once you are standing completely straight up, lower the bar by pushing the hanches back, only slightly bending the genous, unlike when squatting. Conseil : Take a deep breath at the start of le mouvement and keep your poitrine up. Hold your breath as you lower and expirez as you complete le mouvement.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Romanian_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Romanian Deadlift from Deficit', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin standing while holding a bar at arm''s length in front of you. You can stand on a raised platform to increase the range of motion.
2. Begin by flexing the genous slightly, and then flex at the hanche, moving your butt back as far as possible, lowering the torse as far as flexibility allows. The back should remain in absolute extension en permanence, and the bar should remain in contact with the legs. If done properly, there should be heavy tension felt in the ischio-jambiers.
3. Reverse the motion to Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Romanian_Deadlift_from_Deficit/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rope Climb', 'Dos', 'Autre', '1. Grab the rope with both hands above votre tête. Pull down on the rope as you take a small jump.
2. Wrap the rope around one leg, using vos pieds to pinch the rope. Reach up as high as possible with vos bras, gripping the rope tightly.
3. Release the rope from vos pieds as you pull yourself up with vos bras, bringing your genous towards your poitrine.
4. Resecure vos pieds on the rope, and then Levez-vous to take another high hold on the rope. Continue until you reach the top of the rope.
5. To lower yourself, loosen the grip of vos pieds on the rope as you slide down using a hand over hand motion.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Avant-bras, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rope_Climb/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rope Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Kneel 1-2 feet in front of a cable system with a rope attached.
2. After selecting an appropriate poids, grasp the rope with both hands reaching overhead. Your torse should be upright in the position de départ.
3. To begin, flex at the spine, attempting to bring your rib cage to vos jambes as you pull the cable down.
4. Pause at the bottom of the motion, and then Lentement, Revenez en position de départ.
